,title,link,text,language,family
0,Movima language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Movima_language,"It is considered a language isolate, as it has not been proven to be related to any other language. Movima is spoken in the locations of 18 de Noviembre, 20 de Enero, Bella Flor, Buen Día, Carmen de Iruyañez, Carnavales, Ipimo, Miraflores, Navidad, San Lorenzo, and the town of Santa Ana del Yacuma. [1] .",Movima,Language isolate
1,Movima language - Wikipedia - BME,https://static.hlt.bme.hu/semantics/external/pages/jokuc/en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Movima_language.html,"Movima is a language that is spoken by about 1,400 (nearly half) of the Movima, a group of Native Americans that resides in the Llanos de Moxos region of the Bolivian Amazon, in northeastern Bolivia. It is considered a language isolate, as it has not been proven to be related to any other language. Contents 1Phonology 2Morphology 3See also ...",Movima,Language isolate
2,"Movima Language (MZP) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map ...",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/mzp/,Movima is an endangered indigenous language of Bolivia. It is an isolate that is not known to be related to any other language. The language is used as a first language by older adults only. It is not known to be taught in schools.,Movima,Language isolate
3,Movima Phoneme Inventory — IPA Lookup,https://ipalookup.com/languages/movima,Movima (Language isolate) has 29 phonemes. Browse its full IPA sound inventory and compare it to other languages.,Movima,Language isolate
4,Language Phoneme Inventories — IPA Lookup,https://ipalookup.com/languages,"Click any language to browse its full sound system, or use the filters to explore by region or language family. Browse IPA phoneme inventories for 500+ languages. Filter by language family or region, compare sound systems, and explore what consonants and vowels each language uses.",Movima,Language isolate
5,Movima language - Detailed Pedia,https://www.detailedpedia.com/wiki-Movima_language,"Movima is a language that is spoken by about 1,400 (nearly half) of the Movima, a group of Native Americans that resides in the Llanos de Moxos region of the Bolivian Amazon, in northeastern Bolivia. It is considered a language isolate, as it has not been proven to be related to any other language.",Movima,Language isolate
6,Movima language explained,https://everything.explained.today/Movima_language/,"Movima is a language that is spoken by about 1,400 (nearly half) of the Movima, a group of Native Americans that resides in the Llanos de Moxos region of the Bolivia n Amazon, in northeastern Bolivia. It is considered a language isolate, as it has not been proven to be related to any other language.",Movima,Language isolate
7,An Austronesian-type voice system in an Amazonian isolate?,https://hal.science/hal-04211901v2/document,"Movima is an endangered language, still spoken by a few hundred adults, but not transmitted as a first language anymore. Today, the large majority of Movima speakers lives in the town Santa Ana del Yacuma, a former Jesuit mission in the Bolivian department Beni.",Movima,Language isolate
